  "reasoning": "The claim was denied under CO-97 (bundling), which is a medical policy denial rather than a data or documentation error, making resubmission or providing records ineffective. The payer offers peer-to-peer review, and historical data shows that appealing with medical necessity has the highest success rate (4/6) compared to peer-to-peer (3/8) for similar cases. Therefore, filing a formal appeal with a medical-necessity argument is the most statistically robust next step to overturn the bundling denial.",
